      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your pursuit of dignity through a graceful exit is understandable when the art feels like a betrayal of past achievements. However, true legacy is often built not on early peaks, but on the courage to rebuild despite the fear of decline. Choosing to sit on your laurels condemns you to a slow loss of self-worth that the hard work of reinvention could have saved. The most poignant stories are not those that fade quietly, but those that evolve through difficult truths back into something authentic.",
